{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00116",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.83,
      "end_seconds": 4.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Excuse me, doctor, should I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.03,
      "end_seconds": 10.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.3,
      "end_seconds": 18.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "Doctor, it's aching in my thighs. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 20.88,
      "end_seconds": 29.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 119 over 74, pulse 83, saturation 98 percent, temperature is 36.6 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.79,
      "end_seconds": 35.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "okay, noted when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.14,
      "end_seconds": 43.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "About... well, about four days. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.11,
      "end_seconds": 50.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.21,
      "end_seconds": 61.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "Rest helps a bit. It's worse with climbing stairs. It's mild, honestly. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.79,
      "end_seconds": 66.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.11,
      "end_seconds": 76.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "It usually comes with dark urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.16,
      "end_seconds": 82.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "I was just gonna say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 82.31,
      "end_seconds": 88.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.87,
      "end_seconds": 92.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.91,
      "end_seconds": 95.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "And tiredness, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.43,
      "end_seconds": 103.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "have you had aching in your thighs before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.11,
      "end_seconds": 113.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened a couple of years ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 117.77,
      "end_seconds": 119.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.21,
      "end_seconds": 126.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any joint swelling or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.18,
      "end_seconds": 131.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Yeah, no, I'd have mentioned it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.11,
      "end_seconds": 137.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Have you noticed recent heavy exercise, fever or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.62,
      "end_seconds": 142.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "No, no recent heavy exercise, fever or numbness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.6,
      "end_seconds": 146.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.47,
      "end_seconds": 149.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.97,
      "end_seconds": 155.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.81,
      "end_seconds": 158.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.63,
      "end_seconds": 163.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Right, before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.23,
      "end_seconds": 178.54,
      "duration_seconds": 13.31,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.32,
      "end_seconds": 181.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.91,
      "end_seconds": 201.86,
      "duration_seconds": 18.95,
      "text": "Telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. Atorvastatin. I take it 20 milligrams, at night. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. It's Thyronorm, 50 micrograms, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.64,
      "end_seconds": 210.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.3,
      "end_seconds": 217.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "not with me. I'll bring it next time. Rosuvastatin I don't take anymore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.93,
      "end_seconds": 221.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "any surgery in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.86,
      "end_seconds": 224.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Just my gallbladder removed, in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.93,
      "end_seconds": 230.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "tell me about your health in general, any ongoing conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.03,
      "end_seconds": 243.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for five years. I've had high cholesterol for about a year now. I have an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.88,
      "end_seconds": 254.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Okay, I can see an underactive thyroid in your file as well. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.15,
      "end_seconds": 271.46,
      "duration_seconds": 15.31,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend. No, I don't smoke and never have. I'm mostly vegetarian. I go to the gym a couple of times a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.11,
      "end_seconds": 276.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.01,
      "end_seconds": 278.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.44,
      "end_seconds": 295.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "The The muscles are mildly tender when I squeeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.2,
      "end_seconds": 298.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.75,
      "end_seconds": 317.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Power in the thighs is slightly reduced, four out of five."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.33,
      "end_seconds": 325.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Right, you can sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.08,
      "end_seconds": 359.28,
      "duration_seconds": 17.2,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, it fits best with muscle symptoms that may be related to the cholesterol tablet. An underactive thyroid is also on my list. A vitamin D deficiency is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.59,
      "end_seconds": 363.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "do you think it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.08,
      "end_seconds": 374.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.88,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with muscle symptoms that may be related to the cholesterol tablet do well once it's treated properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.6,
      "end_seconds": 396.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a thyroid test for muscle weakness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 397.78,
      "end_seconds": 402.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "we have a slot Wednesday at 10 am, if that that works"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.34,
      "end_seconds": 432.26,
      "duration_seconds": 27.92,
      "text": "I'll request a creatine kinase level, it'll help with muscle pain. I'll request a vitamin D level, it'll help with muscle weakness. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Don't stop any of your tablets on your own, we'll decide after the blood test. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.45,
      "end_seconds": 442.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "the thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse if that happens, go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 443.87,
      "end_seconds": 445.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Okay, I'll remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 447.42,
      "end_seconds": 450.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I'd like you back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.97,
      "end_seconds": 453.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Sure, that's doable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.17,
      "end_seconds": 457.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Alright, I'll see you out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.72,
      "end_seconds": 462.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.5,
      "end_seconds": 465.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ]
}